.\" Manual page of emuled. Keep it aligned with `emuled --help` and docs/MANUAL.md (section B5): the test "manpage" checks the options.
.TH EMULED 1 "2026-10-28" "emuled" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
emuled \- eMule for Linux: eD2K/Kademlia daemon with a REST/WebSocket API and a web interface
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B emuled
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B emuled \-\-setup
.br
.B emuled \-\-install\-service
|
.B \-\-uninstall\-service
.br
.B emuled
.RB [ \-\-profile
.IR DIR ]
.B \-\-reset\-user
.br
.B emuled
.RB [ \-\-profile
.IR DIR ]
.RB ( \-\-check\-profile " | " \-\-scan\-shared " | " \-\-verify\-hashes " | " \-\-update\-known " | " \-\-recover " | " \-\-guard\-scan " | " \-\-guard\-restore )
.RB [ \-\-pathmap
.IR WIN=LINUX ]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B emuled
is the engine of eMule rebuilt as a Linux daemon. It keeps the eMule protocol and the profile file formats of eMule for Windows,
and is driven from a web page (or any HTTP client) through a REST and WebSocket API, by default on
.IR http://127.0.0.1:8765 .
.PP
Run without options from a terminal, when no configuration exists yet, it starts a short
.B wizard
that asks the listen address, the port and the data folder, writes
.I ~/.emuled/config.yaml
and can install emuled as a systemd user service. Without a terminal (systemd, Docker) or with any option, the wizard is skipped.
.PP
The first time the web page is opened it asks to create an account, with the one-time setup code that emuled prints
(with the service:
.BR "journalctl \-\-user \-u emuled" ).
.SH SERVICE AND ACCOUNT
.TP
.B \-\-setup
Run the terminal wizard again (an existing configuration is kept as a .bak copy).
.TP
.B \-\-install\-service
Install and start the systemd user service without questions: writes
.I ~/.config/systemd/user/emuled.service
unless the package already provides the unit, then runs
.BR "systemctl \-\-user enable \-\-now emuled" .
.TP
.B \-\-uninstall\-service
Stop and disable the service and remove the unit written by emuled. The profile and the configuration are not touched.
.TP
.B \-\-reset\-user
Create or reset the user name and password of the web interface (asked in the terminal). Sessions already open are closed.
.SH DAEMON OPTIONS
Command-line options win over environment variables, which win over the configuration file.
.TP
.BI \-\-conf " FILE"
Configuration file to read instead of
.IR ~/.emuled/config.yaml .
.TP
.BI \-\-profile " DIR"
Profile folder (the eMule "config" folder, with
.IR preferences.dat ).
.TP
.BI \-\-api\-port " PORT"
Port of the API and of the web interface (default 8765).
.TP
.BI \-\-api\-bind " ADDRESS"
Address to listen on (default 127.0.0.1). With 0.0.0.0 the API is reachable from the whole network.
.TP
.BI \-\-api\-token " TOKEN"
Use this token instead of the one in
.IR <profile>/emuled.token .
.TP
.B \-\-no\-api
Do not start the API and the web interface.
.TP
.BI \-\-templates\-dir " DIR"
Extra folder of web interface templates (for development).
.TP
.BI \-\-web\-dir " DIR"
Serve a single web interface from this folder instead of the templates.
.TP
.BI \-\-tcp\-port " PORT" "\fR, \fP\-\-udp\-port " PORT
eD2K ports for this run (the usual ones are 55662 TCP and 55672 UDP).
.TP
.BI \-\-server " IP:PORT"
Connect to this server.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-kad
Do not start Kademlia.
.TP
.B \-\-offline
Do not connect to any network (for tests).
.TP
.B \-\-fake\-profile
Temporary identity and preferences that are not saved (for tests).
.TP
.BI \-\-add " LINK"
Add an ed2k:// link at start (can be repeated).
.TP
.BI \-\-pathmap " WIN=LINUX"
Translate a Windows path written in the profile, for example
.BR "\-\-pathmap 'Y:\e\eMule=/home/you/eMule'" .
Can be repeated.
.TP
.BI \-\-max\-seconds " N"
Stop after N seconds.
.TP
.BI \-\-status\-interval " N"
Print a status line every N seconds.
.TP
.B \-\-verbose
More messages in the terminal.
.SH PROFILE TOOLS
They work on the profile given with
.BR \-\-profile .
The read-only ones do not take the lock and never write.
.TP
.B \-\-check\-profile
Read-only: validate the .met files and say what could be recovered. Exit code 0 all healthy, 1 damaged, 2 usage error.
.TP
.B \-\-scan\-shared
Read-only: list the shared files, how many are already known and how many must be hashed.
.TP
.B \-\-verify\-hashes \fR[\fB\-\-sample\fR \fIN\fR] [\fB\-\-max\-size\-mb\fR \fIM\fR]
Read-only: recompute the ed2k and AICH hashes of a sample of the shared files and compare them with known.met.
.TP
.B \-\-update\-known \fR[\fB\-\-force\fR]
Hash the new shared files and update known.met safely.
.TP
.B \-\-recover \fR[\fB\-\-force\fR]
Restore damaged .met files from their .bak copies (the damaged file becomes .corrupt).
.TP
.BI \-\-guard\-scan " " \-\-backup\-dir " DIR"
Save the healthy .part.met files of Temp in DIR (reads Temp only).
.TP
.BI \-\-guard\-restore " SLOT " \-\-backup\-dir " DIR" " \fR[\fP\-\-force\fR]"
Restore a damaged download slot from the most advanced healthy copy.
.TP
.B \-\-force
With \-\-recover and \-\-update\-known: go on even if files were modified in the last 2 minutes (another eMule may be active).
.PP
Network diagnostic probes (\-\-search, \-\-download, \-\-probe\-kad, \-\-probe\-server, \-\-check\-ports, \-\-upnp\-discover, ...)
go out on the real network and are described in the manual.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B EMULED_CONF
Configuration file (like \-\-conf).
.TP
.B EMULED_CONFIG
Profile folder (like \-\-profile).
.TP
.BR EMULED_API_PORT ", " EMULED_API_BIND
Port and address of the API.
.TP
.BR EMULED_TEMPLATES_DIR ", " EMULED_WEB_DIR ", " EMULED_MEDIAINFO
Templates folder, single web interface folder, path of the mediainfo program.
.TP
.B EMULED_LANG
With a value starting with "it" the terminal wizard speaks Italian.
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
No colours in the start-up header.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.emuled/config.yaml
Base configuration (keys config, api_port, api_bind, web_dir, templates_dir, mediainfo).
.TP
.I ~/.emuled/profile/
Default profile: eMule files, emuled.token, emuled.users.
.TP
.I ~/.emuled/templates/
Web interface templates of the user.
.TP
.I ~/.emuled/logs/emuled.log
Log file.
.TP
.I /usr/share/emuled/templates/
Built-in templates.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/systemd/user/emuled.service
User service installed by the package.
.SH SIGNALS
.TP
.B SIGHUP
Recheck the shared folders
.RB ( "systemctl \-\-user reload emuled" ).
.TP
.BR SIGTERM ", " SIGINT
Orderly shutdown (files are saved).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR journalctl (1).
Full manual: /usr/share/doc/emuled/MANUAL.md; API: /usr/share/doc/emuled/APIDOC.md; https://github.com/klode82/emuled
